<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ekpoma</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ekpoma is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-state">Edo State</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, the headquarters of the Esan West local government area. It was one of the Esan chiefdoms whose rulers, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/onojie">Enijie</a>, traced their origins to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Kingdom of Benin</a>. It is home to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambrose">Ambrose</a> Alli University, founded in 1981.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ekpoma.jpg" alt="Ekpoma" width="320" height="280" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Omorodion1 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ekpoma.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
